<h1 class="article-title">Decisions Adopted by the Liepāja SEZ Board on 18 October</h1>
<div class="block_text mt-5 mb-4">
<div class="row">
<div class="col"><div class="col-12 output"><p>At its regular meeting on 18 October 2024, the Liepāja SEZ Board granted Liepāja SEZ company status to BALTU Terminals, supported five investment projects by SEZ companies totalling just under EUR 1 million and amended port charges and building-rights agreements.</p><p>Port charges. In accordance with Cabinet Regulation No. 256 of 23 May 2023, the Authority annually reviews whether port fees and service tariff limits require adjustment. Analysis of European Central Bank consumer price index data for January–August 2024 showed an average index of 2.30% for Latvia’s transport sector, indicating rising costs. As these affect all areas of port operations, a corresponding increase in charges was proposed. To maintain competitive conditions relative to other Latvian ports, the Authority submitted a proposal to increase the channel fee by two euro cents. The Board reviewed and approved this amendment.</p><p>The Board also approved a two-euro-cent increase in the charge for using common port infrastructure and related facilities per tonne of cargo loaded or unloaded. The proposed changes were discussed and agreed with companies operating in the Port of Liepāja and took effect on 1 January 2025.</p><p>Liepāja SEZ company status. The Authority received an application from BALTU Terminals requesting SEZ company status and an agreement to conduct business in the zone. After reviewing the documents, the Board decided to grant the status.</p><p>Implementation of investment projects. The Board supported five investment projects by SEZ companies worth EUR 925,110 in total. Jensen Metal plans to acquire modern technical equipment for its new production building at 11 Virssardzes Street, Liepāja, between 22 October 2024 and 31 December 2025, investing EUR 410,000.00. Jensen Metal also plans another project with the same title and implementation period worth EUR 52,000.00.</p><p>AE Partner plans to purchase measuring instruments between 23 October 2024 and 1 February 2025 for EUR 8,500.00. Northside Business Park plans to purchase two overhead cranes for Production Building No. 19 between 1 November and 31 December 2024 for EUR 36,300.00.</p><p>BALTU Terminals plans to purchase machinery and equipment for stevedoring services from 1 November 2024 to 31 March 2025, for EUR 418,310.00.</p><p>In 2023, the Authority concluded 15 investment agreements with Liepāja SEZ companies, with planned investments totalling EUR 5,481,903.28.</p><p>By 1 October 2024, the Authority had concluded 14 agreements for investment in modern technology and construction, with planned investments totalling EUR 16,864,976.</p><p>Amendments to building-rights agreements. The Board decided to amend the agreement with MOLS L to add the construction projects “New Bulk Cargo Warehouse” and “Construction of Railway Scales”, setting 31 December 2026 as the completion deadline.</p><p>The Board also decided to amend the building-rights agreement of 1 March 2019 with Karosta LP, setting 31 December 2027 as the deadline for completion of all construction projects included in it.</p></div>
